er who prioritizes expensive, robust safety engineering will be outcompeted by one who cuts corners, unless those safety standards are mandated internationally. We must move beyond the fantasy that market incentives alone will prevent the pursuit of capabilities that maximize competitive advantage at the expense of our collective existence.",
